'''Scott Fox''' (December 28, 1963 – June 16, 2015)<ref name=":0">{{Cite news |date=2015-06-21 |title=Obituary for SCOTT FOX |url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-tennessean-obituary-for-scott-fox/183307484/ |access-date=2025-10-19 |work=[[The Tennessean]] |pages=17A |via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}</ref> was an American professional [[American football|football]] [[linebacker]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He was a [[replacement player]] for the [[Houston Oilers]] during the [[National Football League Players Association#1987 strike and decertification|players strike]] in the [[1987 NFL season]]. He played football at Clinton Senior High School in [[Clinton, Tennessee]], graduating in 1981.  He played [[college football]] at [[Austin Peay State University|Austin Peay State]]. He was 6'2" and weighed 222&nbsp;lbs. in his playing time. {{Citation needed|date=October 2025}}
